{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"af5f83ff6aa8c389924c778cb76ad61b9a4858aecf14a27bacfec449ee79b30c","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar-gerrit alerting and terraform IaC pipeline","key_entities":["rebar-gerrit-alerts SNS topic","aws_cloudwatch_metric_alarm.gerrit_data_disk_high","rebar-terraform-plan IAM role",".github/workflows/terraform-drift.yml","infra/terraform/iam.tf","infra/terraform/monitoring.tf","token.actions.githubusercontent.com OIDC provider","account 896586841071"],"problem_keywords":["terraform drift","infrastructure as code","alerting","SNS subscription","CloudWatch alarm","CI/CD","OIDC authentication","state management"],"propositions":["CloudWatch alarms committed to HCL can remain unapplied indefinitely without detection, causing silent gaps in alert coverage (dc3f root cause).","One live alarm (rebar-gerrit-data-disk-high) exists in AWS but is absent from HCL/state with an empty alarm_actions list, so it never notifies.","GitHub OIDC-based terraform plan CI does not exist, requiring manual apply steps that allow drift between committed HCL and live infrastructure to go unnoticed.","The SNS subscription for rebar-gerrit-alerts must be confirmed (not PendingConfirmation) to ensure alarms actually deliver to recipients.","A least-privilege IAM role is needed for GitHub Actions to run read-only terraform plans via OIDC without write permissions or state locking."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785824097484589932,"uuid":"15890d38-abf2-4e93-9207-a178b497b939"}